      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, overall these  hw timers are not really designed to be re-clocked while running.\nThis was kind of a best-effort update to be wrong less 1 time of one billion rather than consistently wrong,\nwe can add even more complexity here, but the proper solution to be 100% correct is actually to update the upstream clock divider and keep the input clock frequency constant.\nAs soon as I have benchmarked the application to find which clock rates are suiting my needs, I will switch my board to such a system.\nI might just add comment here (actually none of our systems are re-clocking more than once after startup)",
